# What NOT to upload as a Cloud Build source context.
#
# Without this the context is the whole working tree — 1.9GB, most of it
# .venv and node_modules — which is uploaded on every build and then ignored
# by the Dockerfile anyway.
#
# gcloud will fall back to .gitignore when this file is absent, which happens
# to produce a similar result today. That is a coincidence of the two files
# agreeing, not a guarantee: .gitignore answers "what should not be committed"
# and this answers "what should not leave the machine". They diverge the moment
# something is committed that a build has no business seeing.

.git/
.gitignore

# Local Python and Node trees. The images install their own dependencies.
.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Credentials. Already covered by .gitignore, repeated here because the cost of
# these two lines being wrong is uploading a Snowflake token to a build service.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local run artifacts.
logs/
*.log
.next/
coverage/
.idea/
.DS_Store
